# EcoSwap CODEOWNERS
#
# Automatically requests reviews from the assigned owner when a PR touches
# files matching the patterns below. Owners are matched in order from top to
# bottom — the LAST matching pattern wins, so more-specific paths go later.
#
# Team mapping (per §6.1 of the planning doc):
#   M1 = @Jedad11    — backend lead (auth, match logic)
#   M2 = @Vannyyoda   — mobile lead (item CRUD, chat)
#   M3 = @Waltzz62  — UX/frontend (feed, QR client)
#   M4 = @PausEzi    — infrastructure (QR backend, impact tracker)
#   M5 = @SittaWetpa — designer + tester, repo owner, PR coordinator
#
# Pair-rotation reviewers (see CLAUDE.md → Pull request review process):
#   @Jedad11 (M1)    ↔ @PausEzi (M4)
#   @PausEzi (M4)    ↔ @Jedad11 (M1)
#   @Vannyyoda (M2)   ↔ @Waltzz62 (M3)
#   @Waltzz62 (M3)  ↔ @Vannyyoda (M2)
#   @SittaWetpa (M5) → cross-cutting; reviewed by workstream pair

# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Default owner — catches anything not matched by a more specific rule.
# M5 acts as fallback / coordinator.
# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
